Z||000001||FieroLisa||12-03-2001||03:24 PM||||When I bought my 86 coupe, I didn't know it needed the tranny rebuilt. Cost me $1200.  Ouch. <P>If this is the first fiero you have looked at, keep looking. There are lots out there lookin for good homes.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>AIM: FieroLisa||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||12-03-2001||03:30 PM||||It depends on whether you're doing the work or paying for someone else's labor. Plan on rolling the dice with $200-300 for a used trans and just under $150 for a clutch pack and turn the flywheel. Add another $500 for the sh1t the last 10 guys cobbled up before you got it. Is it gonna be worth $1200 plus labor when you're done??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I'd pass if I were you.||||reg||13
